The 340 values of kb-abstract in this edition quote the sources D3FEND cites:
patents, papers, articles, manuals and specifications, each named by its
record's kb_reference_title, kb_author and has_link. Those words stay their
authors'. MITRE's licence grants what MITRE holds, and this project grants
nothing over them. So the catalogue leaves them out, and nothing this project
generates holds one. They stay only in upstream/d3fend.ttl, MITRE's file copied
whole and unchanged, as the Terms of Use authorise. Some definitions and
comments also quote a source, and those stay in the catalogue as part of MITRE's
text. Anyone who republishes any of them apart from D3FEND should check with
their authors.

